 "notes": [
  "PROPOSED by Kernel K6, Sound Head, under the 5 m grid rule (10 Nov late note).",
  "Five terraces on the contours at 11, 23, 35 (main street), 47 and 59 m, about 50 m apart: 12 m between terraces leaves room for the 31 degree bank between a row and the next street. Rows are on one side only, buildings at most 12.5 m deep, one level per segment.",
  "The gate square sits on the saddle at the bowl's south-east lip, where the Notch road comes in; the quay is on the shore strip to the north-east.",
  "Lamps are yours.",
  "Stairs (foot only) are not drawn as streets: a stair steeper than the 31 degree bank cannot be graded ground. Build them as stair pieces between terraces: south stair near x 2500-2650, y 10520-10546; middle stair y 10604-10616; north stair y 10668-10678; quay stair from the main street's north end to the quay apron."
